{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/490003-npc-idea-decapitated-head","id":490003,"title":"NPC Idea - Decapitated Head?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-23T16:34:56-07:00","id":490003,"title":"NPC Idea - Decapitated Head?","content":"So I was reading a thread about Beast where somebody brought up Mimir, a Norse God who was decpitated, and whispers secrets and advice to Odin, who carries him around.<br /> <br /> It's quite the image, isn't it? So much so, that I kind of thought that it'd be cool to have an NPC/Prop NPC who is essentially a very wise or mystically mighty Elder who has no body, and spends most of his time as a decapitated head in torpor. For obvious reasons, a coven in the Circle of the Crone comes to mind. I have the idea of Acolytes feeding it Vitae to awaken it for ritual purposes, to dispense advice and the like.<br /> <br /> So, neat idea, but some musings about how possible it actually is: Considering it's been mentioned that the brain is the seat of Kindred Consciousness (not strictly necessary for function, but it hurts them when you shoot it!) and the rest of the body seems to just sort of be there, could a Kindred survive as a decapitated head?<br /> <br /> Moreover, if their Blood Potency sinks low enough, could that head &quot;imbibe&quot; Vitae for the purposes of bringing them out of torpor? What do you guys think of this sort of thing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T16:39:49-07:00","id":490027,"title":"","content":"I think there's a Hunter conspiracy that has a bunch of talking head advisors. They aren't Kindred, as far as I know, just talking heads. I want to say it's Aegis Kai Doru but I don't recall. I'm sure someone else will.<br /> <br /> As for your suggesting vampires, some members of Belial's Brood have an ability that would allow them to detach their heads and sort of walk around on them.<br /> <br /> Belial's Brood, p135, 'Detached heads get about with the \ufb02ailing and serpentine movements of a mass of dangling viscera that separates from the body along with the head. A detached head has full access to the vampire\u2019s blood pool and can make use of any Discipline that doesn\u2019t require a body or gestures. A detached head that fails to reconnect with its body at the end of the scene must spend one additional Vitae per scene, or the vampire will enter involuntary torpor.'<br /> <br /> I suppose it would just be a matter of a devotion or higher Investment that would allow for something more long-lasting. And yes, just getting blood onto its viscera should be as good as getting it into its mouth or eyes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T16:48:00-07:00","id":490055,"title":"","content":"Cool. I wasn't necessarily in need of mechanics for it, since it's really just a fluffy funky NPC, but that's awesome! I'll have to look into picking up the Brood book to see if there's any other cool ideas in there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T20:15:28-07:00","id":490160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/490003-npc-idea-decapitated-head?p=490027#post490027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. . .As for your suggesting vampires, some members of Belial's Brood have an ability that would allow them to detach their heads and sort of walk around on them.<br /> <br /> Belial's Brood, p135, 'Detached heads get about with the \ufb02ailing and serpentine movements of a mass of dangling viscera that separates from the body along with the head. A detached head has full access to the vampire\u2019s blood pool and can make use of any Discipline that doesn\u2019t require a body or gestures. A detached head that fails to reconnect with its body at the end of the scene must spend one additional Vitae per scene, or the vampire will enter involuntary torpor.'<br /> <br /> I suppose it would just be a matter of a devotion or higher Investment that would allow for something more long-lasting. And yes, just getting blood onto its viscera should be as good as getting it into its mouth or eyes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Similar rules were included in <b>Kindred of the East</b>, for kuei-jin who got sloppy with the second level Flesh Shintai power, and lost their bodies. Life as a severed head pretty much sucks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> . . . unless you have other abilities (like Jade Shintai) that let you move without a body <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T21:11:44-07:00","id":490175,"title":"","content":"Yes, it was the Aegis Kai Doru. Apparently they have a think for heads. A lot of the Stereotypes other groups have for them mention that they have the head of John the Baptist in a cave, and it tells them things. Their own write-up seems to suggest that it prophecies disaster. Also in their Compacts and Conspiracies chap, it tells us this, 'Fact: the Aegis Kai Doru have a thing for severed heads. They believe that the severed head contains the soul and wisdom of the body, and that death does not necessarily end the wisdom contained within.' And it offers two head relics, including a pre-Revolution hunter and the head of Jayne Mansfield, rescued from the clutches of a demiurge presumably about to create a Galateid.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/490003-npc-idea-decapitated-head?p=490160#post490160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Similar rules were included in <b>Kindred of the East</b>, for kuei-jin who got sloppy with the second level Flesh Shintai power, and lost their bodies. Life as a severed head pretty much sucks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> . . . unless you have other abilities (like Jade Shintai) that let you move without a body</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been probably twelve years, but I also recall reading some of the Grails Covenant books, and I want to say there was a severed vampire head in there, too, but I don't remember.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T17:14:19-07:00","id":495448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/490003-npc-idea-decapitated-head#post490003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering it's been mentioned that the brain is the seat of Kindred Consciousness (not strictly necessary for function, but it hurts them when you shoot it!) and the rest of the body seems to just sort of be there, could a Kindred survive as a decapitated head?</div> </div> </div> </div>I do agree, the head is the seat of consciousness in the matter of Kindred, but if you stake one through the heart, they go into Torpor\u2014and if you tear one's heart out, it's likely they also go to Final Death. On the other hand . . . there is that one Scale of the Dragon that certain members of the Ordo Dracul can perform, wherein the heart can be safely removed without the subject dying or going Torpid. (Which just makes me think of a deranged decapitated head, wondering where its heart went.)<br /> <br /> I would actually argue this to be a perfect matter for the Dragons instead of the Acolytes. Let's say that certain <i>very</i> knowledgeable members or renegades of the Ordo are considered irredeemable, but just too valuable to simply destroy or condemn to sanctioned Diablerie . . . and instead, their heads are preserved\u2014along with their hearts, perhaps?\u2014and specifically consulted on forbidden or dangerous lore. (If you've ever read the Dark Eldar trilogy from Warhammer 40,000, there's a certain seer who ends up in this sort of situation, kept alive by the twisted science of the Haemonculi covens.)<br /> <br /> Hell, one could even keep the head and heart separate, as a means of security: If someone steals a head, hoping to liberate the renegade or press it for information, whosoever is still in possession of the heart can destroy it to settle the matter (or stake it to render the head into Torpor if they plan on recovering the head instead); and besides that, they can use it as a threat to the head if it doesn't cooperate. That is, of course, aside from whatever tortures could possibly be levied at said disembodied head (again, see the Dark Eldar trilogy). Plenty of story ideas there <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":583,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","user":"Zsander","date":". 05-01-2015, 10:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T18:07:07-07:00","id":495514,"title":"","content":"That's a really compelling idea, and that the Ordo would keep a head like that makes sense to me. I'm imagining a scale where the Heart is kept as a sort of phylactery while the head can be revived. Probably not a popular Scale, most likely used as a punishment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T18:33:04-07:00","id":495577,"title":"","content":"The idea of how little a vampire needs to survive has often come up within my friend group. We, too, seemed to settle on the brain and heart, presumably requiring some method of imbibing vitae.<br /> <br /> Comments were made about perhaps ordo dracul experiments into how much one could remove of a vampire without them dying. Imagine a dragon's lab with a brain and connected heart floating in a large jar of vitae, the pinnacle of their experiments. Around the rest of the room? The diagrams and remaining parts of the failures - those that perhaps didn't survive.<br /> <br /> That said, it certainly fits into many covenants and their related concepts. The image of a head, heart and parts of a shattered ribcage being revered as a sacred artifact or wise leader by a congregation of the circle is absolutely wonderful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1230,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1230-thenagain","user":"thenagain","date":". 04-28-2015, 09:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1230-thenagain","name":"thenagain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T20:10:54-07:00","id":495670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenagain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/490003-npc-idea-decapitated-head?p=495577#post495577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. . . head, heart and parts of a shattered ribcage being revered as a sacred artifact . . .</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget the flaming chain-whip! :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T06:07:54-07:00","id":496211,"title":"","content":"I think you should watch season 3 of American Horror Story to mine ideas on how to create severed heads that still retain sentience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T11:18:13-07:00","id":499138,"title":"","content":"LIIIIIIES!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T05:55:45-07:00","id":501621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zsander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/490003-npc-idea-decapitated-head?p=495670#post495670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't forget the flaming chain-whip! :P</div> </div> </div> </div>I was doggedly resisting the urge to suggest that the Aegis Kai Doru should have a dimwitted redhead thousand-year-old caretaker who looks after their council of heads.<br /> <br /> Then you posted <i>that</i>^<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T14:24:18-07:00","id":506080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenagain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/490003-npc-idea-decapitated-head?p=495577#post495577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea of how little a vampire needs to survive has often come up within my friend group. We, too, seemed to settle on the brain and heart, presumably requiring some method of imbibing vitae.<br /> <br /> Comments were made about perhaps ordo dracul experiments into how much one could remove of a vampire without them dying. Imagine a dragon's lab with a brain and connected heart floating in a large jar of vitae, the pinnacle of their experiments. Around the rest of the room? The diagrams and remaining parts of the failures - those that perhaps didn't survive.<br /> <br /> That said, it certainly fits into many covenants and their related concepts. The image of a head, heart and parts of a shattered ribcage being revered as a sacred artifact or wise leader by a congregation of the circle is absolutely wonderful.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a character in the Mekhet book with no brain. She was mummified before embrace so the brain was taken out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2191-kevorkiandoctor","name":"Kevorkiandoctor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T16:07:00-07:00","id":506156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kevorkiandoctor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/490003-npc-idea-decapitated-head?p=506080#post506080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a character in the Mekhet book with no brain. She was mummified before embrace so the brain was taken out</div> </div> </div> </div>'And it made no difference to the Mekhet. Brain or not, you unwrapped the bandages and spilled a few drops of blood in the corpse\u2019s mouth, and your childe gasped and writhed in the wrappings and begged for more.'<br /> <br /> I wonder how far you could take that.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://houseofgeekery.files.wordpress.com/2012/03/tiki-download_file-php.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-06-2015, 07:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T17:17:54-07:00","id":506247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kevorkiandoctor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/490003-npc-idea-decapitated-head?p=506080#post506080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is a character in the Mekhet book with no brain. She was mummified before embrace so the brain was taken out</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, she's delusional and was wrong about the date of her embrace by a couple of thousand years, so that's not necessarily true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;These are merely stones...&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/276-merkonan","name":"Merkonan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar276_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T18:34:30-07:00","id":506299,"title":"","content":"Just one thousand. And she may be a weird case of memory swiping, as there was a vampire raised as Nitokris in Egypt when she claims. But in second edition the posthumous embrace doesn't seem to require a brain, just to be done 'before significant decomposition sets in.' It can be performed regardless of the cause of death, providing they've fed from a vampire.<br /> <br /> I think decapitation would eliminate chances of it working, but perhaps not if you sewed the head back on quick enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-06-2015, 09:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T18:37:00-07:00","id":506300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kevorkiandoctor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/490003-npc-idea-decapitated-head?p=506080#post506080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is a character in the Mekhet book with no brain. She was mummified before embrace so the brain was taken out</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what she <b>claims</b> - that said, the actual truthfulness of anything said by Nitokris is of very debatable reliability indeed.<br /> Check out Francis Black's glass harmonion-induced visions for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T17:43:50-07:00","id":508573,"title":"","content":"As everybody else said, that's what she claims.<br /> <br /> Whether or not a brain is required is up for debate - not a debate I really care about, run it how you want in your game. I'm very up for the idea of vampire's bodies being essentially unnecessary, (something which 2nd Ed resilience really lends itself to) but then you start getting into the business of how a vampire works, where their mind/self/consciousness is stored and I can't be dealing with defining that sort of metaphysics for a forum post. Besides, the image of a floating brain in a jar is clearly more evocative ;D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1230-thenagain","name":"thenagain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}